<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Giản Định Đế</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 1407–<a href="/years/1409">1409</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Trần Ngỗi, Gian Dinh De</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Giản Định Đế, born Trần Ngỗi, was a son of the Trần emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tran-nghe-tong">Trần Nghệ Tông</a>. After the Ming conquest of the Hồ dynasty in 1407 he proclaimed himself emperor in Ninh Bình and led the Later Trần resistance, winning a victory at Bô Cô in 1408. Quarrels among his commanders brought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tran-quy-khoang">Trùng Quang</a> Đế to the throne, and he was later captured by the Ming.</p></div>
